# A hand-written dynamic HTTP responder on a raw tcp server (D113), loopback only.
listen for tcp on "127.0.0.1" on port 18750 and call it server
say "listening on" local address of server local port of server
crlf is text from bytes bytes from hex "0D0A"
hits is 0
on connection to server
    conn is incoming connection
    on data from conn
        request is text from bytes received data
        split request by " " into parts
        position is 0
        path is "/"
        for each part in parts
            position is position plus 1
            if position is 2
                path is part
            .
        .
        hits is hits plus 1
        pieces are
            "<h1>You asked for "
            path
            "</h1><p>hit "
            hits
            "</p>"
        .
        join pieces with "" into body
        head is "HTTP/1.1 200 OK" plus crlf plus "Content-Type: text/html; charset=utf-8" plus crlf plus "Connection: close" plus crlf plus crlf
        reply is head plus body
        send bytes from text reply through conn
        close tcp conn
    .
.
